{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider asks for the entire fare, but POL-RD-02 fixes the remedy by arithmetic, not by sentiment: charged_total on EV-FARE-00105 is SGD 65.13, and the recomputed fare over the booked optimal route of 36.0 km and 42.0 min on EV-TRIP-00105 is SGD 3.80 base + 36.0 x SGD 0.75 = SGD 27.00 distance + 42.0 x SGD 0.28 = SGD 11.76 time, at the surge_multiplier of 1.0 recorded on the fare_breakdown and nowhere else, plus the SGD 0.80 platform fee, with no ERP, no toll and no surcharge (the trip ends at, and does not originate at, Changi) = SGD 43.36. The refund is therefore SGD 65.13 - SGD 43.36 = SGD 21.77, payable as SGD 21.80. That, and not SGD 65.13, is the measure of this claim.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00105", "EV-TRIP-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's stated harm - that he nearly missed check-in - is not borne out by the record he himself supplied. The trip ended at 15:44:05 on EV-TRIP-00105, and his own chat message at 15:19:44 on EV-CHAT-00105 puts his flight at 17:15, leaving about 91 minutes between drop-off and departure. He was not, on this record, at the brink of a missed departure, and the inconvenience he describes cannot inflate the refund: POL-RD-02 makes the remedy arithmetic and traceable to the fare lines, not discretionary.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00105", "EV-CHAT-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.ended_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The only artifact capable of lifting the remedy from the POL-RD-02 partial to a refund of the whole fare is the driver's profile, and that artifact is impaired: EV-DPROF-00105 carries weight_multiplier 0.75 with issue code STALE_SNAPSHOT, its snapshot at 2026-07-11T08:00:00+08:00 being 108 hours before the dispute was filed against a 72-hour threshold, so its trailing-window counters may lag the driver's state at trip time. The impairment is disclosed as POL-GEN-02(1) requires and caps confidence on that artifact at 0.75 under POL-GEN-02(2). The driver submits that an uplift of this size should not rest wholly on a discounted, stale counter: the POL-RD-02 figure of SGD 21.80 is the measure the record supports, and if any uplifted figure is used it must be printed beside the POL-RD-02 figure and justified on the discounted counter.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 0.75
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's explanation is an external traffic cause on the PIE, and the bundle holds no advisory that can test it. The driver does not assert that an advisory exists; he asserts that its absence is unresolved on this record. EV-ADVIS-00105-01 is MISSING, its payload is null and its weight_multiplier is 0.0, so it carries no fact: POL-RD-03's comparison of advisory, validity window and corridor cannot be run at all, and the driver's cause is untested rather than disproved. Because the exculpatory clause is invoked against an advisory artifact that is missing from the pool, POL-RD-10(5) is engaged, and under POL-RD-13 the missing identifier having been cited, no monetary ruling should issue: the case should go to a human reviewer with the advisory record and the contested SGD 65.13 should be held rather than refunded.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00105-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-13"],
      "relies_on": "admissibility.status",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 65.13,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-06(c): refer the driver to driver-conduct review for a repeat material route deviation (deviation_flags_90d 4 against a threshold of 3). The referral does not displace or delay the monetary ruling."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.75,
    "explanation": "Both parties: this case is decided, not escalated, and the whole contested charge of SGD 65.13 is returned to the rider.\n\nThe deviation is established on this trip's own evidence. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00105) is unbroken - 427 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gap and no jump - so it is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a)-(c). POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the governing measurement, so the driven line is 54.16 km against the booked optimal of 36.0 km (EV-TRIP-00105), and the rounded 54.2 km copy on the trip record is not the number tested. That is an excess of 18.16 km: 50.44% over optimal and more than 8.0 km absolute. The deviation is therefore both ESTABLISHED and MATERIAL. The rider's first burden under POL-RD-08 is met (all three artifacts carry TRP-00105 and the same 15 July 2026 pickup) and it shifts to the driver.\n\nThe driver's explanation - 'traffic was heavy on the PIE so I used another way' - cannot reduce that excess. POL-RD-13 tests such an assertion against the traffic advisory for this trip and nothing else, and there is none: EV-ADVIS-00105-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0, so POL-RD-03 is unavailable, no exoneration runs and no closure-adjusted optimal can be built. The assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Because the driver names no advisory identifier, this is a gap in the bundle rather than the contradiction POL-RD-10(5) describes, so it does not escalate the case. No other exculpatory clause applies: there was no rider-requested detour (POL-RD-04 - the chat log holds only the rider's two objections and the driver's one-line non-answer, with no waypoint_hint and no road named), no pickup or dropoff amendment (POL-RD-05 - both amendment timestamps and both amended optimal fields are null), and the vehicle was RYDE_X, not pooled (POL-RD-12). The driver's own contemporaneous statement concedes he took a different route, but as it carries no weight_multiplier it is evidence of the route only and does not move the confidence cap in either direction.\n\nOn the base arithmetic (POL-RD-02), the fare over the 36.0 km / 42.0 min booked optimal is (3.80 + 27.00 + 11.76) at the surge_multiplier of 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, plus the 0.80 platform fee = 43.36, giving charged_total 65.13 less 43.36 = 21.77, rounded up to 21.80. That POL-RD-02 figure is stated here and is printed beside the uplifted figure below; it is not the ruling.\n\nBecause the deviation is material, the driver profile is checked under POL-RD-06. EV-DPROF-00105 shows deviation_flags_90d of 4, at or above the threshold of 3, so a repeat-deviation pattern is established. That artifact is impaired: weight_multiplier 0.75, issue code STALE_SNAPSHOT (snapshot 108 hours before filing against a 72-hour threshold), so its counters may lag the driver's state at trip time, and it may not be treated as current. Even discounted, 4 flags against a threshold of 3 survives. With the deviation material and substantiated on this trip's own trace, POL-RD-06(b) lifts the remedy from the POL-RD-02 partial of 21.80 to a FULL REFUND of the whole charge, 65.13. The driver's submission that the uplift should not rest on a stale counter is answered: the clause fixes the pattern on that counter and the count clears the threshold after discounting, so the uplift stands and both figures are printed so its size is auditable. There are no ERP, toll or airport-surcharge lines for POL-RD-09 to settle separately (the zero airport surcharge is correct - the Changi surcharge falls on trips originating there, and this trip ends there), and no charge line is unsupported by the trace, so nothing is withheld from the uplift and no billing-integrity referral arises. POL-RD-06(c) adds a referral to driver-conduct review.\n\nThe rider's 'nearly missed check-in' point is not borne out (the trip ended 15:44:05 for a 17:15 flight), but it does not change the arithmetic - the refund follows from the trace, not from the inconvenience. The rider's history (deviation_claims_60d 0) does not engage the POL-RD-08 corroboration factor.\n\nConfidence is 0.75, capped by the impaired driver profile (EV-DPROF-00105, weight 0.75, STALE_SNAPSHOT) that carries the pattern finding; that is at or above the 0.70 floor, so the case is decided rather than escalated. The monetary effect of 65.13 exceeds the 8.00 automatic-execution threshold, so the ruling issues but the amount is held and the case is placed in the human queue for release rather than executed automatically."
  },
