    "explanation": "To both parties. The deviation is established and it is material. EV-GPS-00105 is unbroken — 427 fixes at a 10-second sample interval, 100% coverage, largest gap 0.0 s — so it is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a)–(c). POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the governing figure: 54.16 km driven against the booked optimal of 36.0 km on EV-TRIP-00105 is an excess of 18.16 km, or 50.44%. That clears both establishment limbs (over 0.8 km and over 20%) and both materiality limbs (over 8.0 km and over 50%). The trip record's 54.2 km is a rounded copy of the same measurement and is not the number the threshold test runs on. Nothing excuses any part of the excess: EV-CHAT-00105 holds only two rider objections and a driver non-answer, neither rider message carries a waypoint_hint or names a road, so POL-RD-04 has no instruction to corroborate and excludes no distance; POL-RD-05 cannot run (pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null, amended_optimal_distance_km is null); POL-RD-12 does not apply (vehicle_type RYDE_X, solo_optimal_distance_km null); and POL-RD-11 does not close the distance route (fare_model METERED, quoted_fare_sgd null), so the rider did bear the detour on the distance and time lines. The driver's own statement concedes he took another way, and the trace shows a deliberate line rather than lane-level navigation. The traffic explanation is discarded: EV-ADVIS-00105-01 is MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, and no advisory covers the PIE eastbound in the 14:26–15:44 window. Under POL-RD-13 that assertion is tested against the advisory for this trip and nothing else; with no advisory on file POL-RD-03 is unavailable and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. No identifier was cited for it, so this is a gap in the bundle rather than a POL-RD-10(5) contradiction, and it does not escalate. On the money: the POL-RD-02 recomputation against the booked optimal is (SGD 3.80 base + 0.75 x 36.0 km + 0.28 x 42.0 min) x the surge multiplier of 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, plus the SGD 0.80 platform fee = SGD 42.56 + SGD 0.80 = SGD 43.36. Charged_total is SGD 65.13, so the POL-RD-02 refund would be SGD 65.13 - SGD 43.36 = SGD 21.77, payable as SGD 21.80 — 33.4% of the charge. There is no ERP, toll, surcharge, waiting fee or promo, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing and nothing is double-counted. But the remedy is not the partial. The deviation is MATERIAL and substantiated on this trip's own trace, and the driver profile establishes a repeat pattern on the only field POL-RD-06 permits: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 4, at or above the threshold of 3 (the 90-day ratio, 4/344 = 0.012, is below 0.05, but the counter test alone is sufficient). The impairment is named as POL-GEN-02(3) requires: EV-DPROF-00105 is IMPAIRED, weight_multiplier 0.75, issue code STALE_SNAPSHOT — its snapshot is 108 hours before filing against a 72-hour threshold, so the trailing counters may lag the driver's state at trip time. The pattern finding survives the discount: 4 flags against a threshold of 3 remains above the line, so the counter is not treated as current but the finding stands. POL-RD-06(b) therefore lifts the remedy from the POL-RD-02 partial of SGD 21.80 to FULL_REFUND of charged_total, SGD 65.13. The two figures are stated side by side so the size of the uplift (SGD 43.36) is auditable; no government-set or third-party pass-through line exists for POL-RD-09 to settle separately, so the whole SGD 65.13 moves. Confidence is capped at 0.75, the minimum weight among the artifacts carrying the deciding facts: the deviation at full weight on EV-GPS-00105 (1.0), and the repeat pattern that lifts the remedy, carried solely by EV-DPROF-00105 at 0.75. That is above the 0.70 floor, so the case is decided rather than escalated; no POL-RD-10 trigger fires (all three artifacts carry TRP-00105, no POL-RD-07 trace impairment, no timestamp conflict, no refund above SGD 150.00). On the driver's surviving points: the observation that the rider was not at the brink of a missed flight is accepted — drop-off was 15:44:05 and his own message puts the flight at 17:15, about 91 minutes — but the refund is arithmetic and does not turn on it; the submission that SGD 21.80 is the measure is rejected for the POL-RD-06(b) reason above. On the rider's account of his own history: rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so no extra corroboration is required and POL-GEN-01 confines the profile to that one test. POL-RD-06(c) adds the driver-conduct referral recorded above; it is a referral and does not delay the money. Because the monetary effect (SGD 65.13) exceeds the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, this provisional ruling is issued but not executed: the amount is held for human release. Either party may appeal within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
